<div class="wp-block-group oa-choose"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"sp-reveal sp-reveal--up"} -->
<p class="sp-reveal sp-reveal--up">Choose the H2 when the sound has to stay with you: night, travel, a phone in a shared room. It leaks very little, and the character is close and warm, with firm bass. Choose the H1 when you want air and width and light bass, and a leak into the room is acceptable. Any phone or DAC is enough.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"sp-reveal sp-reveal--up"} -->
<p class="sp-reveal sp-reveal--up">Choose the P7 when you want an even, detailed sound and deep bass, and you can use the A10 or the A40. It is the heaviest of the three at 420 g, and it is open-back, so it leaks. Hearing all three at the same volume is more useful than ranking the ohms.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
